<title>EGYPT: Yield rises on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield rises on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills rose to 10.259 percent from 10.249 percent at the previous auction on August 26.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Mar 2, 1997 (Feb 25, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 10.259 percent (10.249)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 629.625 milion (977.950 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 752.325 million (1.003 billion)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 10.101-10.284 percent (10.101-10.291)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 10.101-10.600 percent (10.101-10.600)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 202 (208)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 212 (2159)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.40 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
